CARD ATTACK
A Strange Query demo for Demosplash 2026
CARDIAC on macOS on Apple Silicon

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every pixel and every sample of sound is computed live on CARDIACs, the
1968 Bell Labs cardboard computer, emulated by HEARTBURN on every core. Every
machine is written in Rust and compiled to CARDIAC with rust-cardiac.  
See https://strangequery.com/cardiac/demos/card-attack after the shows
for more information. 

PLATFORM
--------
CARDIAC / macOS (HEARTBURN emulator running on macOS) 

TECHNIQUE
---------
This demo shows off the CARDIAC cardboard computer's ability to run a compo.
100% of the audio and video in this demo runs on CARDIAC. Most of the code 
was written in Rust that was compiled via Strange Query's rust-cardiac 
into cardiac instructions. A few critical machines are hand-tuned
CARDIAC assembly for space / performance reasons. HEARTBURN on a Mac
runs about five billion times faster than a human on each core, and it 
uses ~28 cores on the Mac Studio being used to present. It should be
possible to run on other hardware but CARD ATTACK is very computationally
demanding, so no guarantees the demo will successfully render in real-time. 

Audio is shipped via two CARDIAC tracks (left.track and right.track) that were 
rendered by the "stage" program in Strange Query's "lubdub" project. These 
tracks are rendered in real time into stereo audio via two CARDIACs, using the 
decoder from Strange Query's "lubdub" project. 

All of this is managed by a host program whose only job is shuttling inputs 
and outputs between machines. The diagram below gives the rough architecture.

 PICTURES: 12 frames a second

   decks         +---------+   +---------+          +---------+
   (programs --> | CARDIAC |   | CARDIAC |   ....   | CARDIAC |  28 workers,
    + data)      +---------+   +---------+          +---------+  one HEARTBURN
                   |    ^        |    ^               |    ^     on each
                   v    |        v    |               v    |
                 +--------------------------------------------+
                 |  host: deals cards in, collects cards out, |
                 |  passes each machine's output to the next  |
                 +--------------------------------------------+
                                      |
                                      v
                 +--------------------------------------------+
                 |  composer CARDIACs: put together each      |
                 |  frame of the cut                          |
                 +--------------------------------------------+
                                      |
                                      v
                                  pixels out

 SOUND: 48,000 samples a second

   left.track   --> [ CARDIAC: lubdub decoder ] --> left  --+
                                                            +--> stereo out
   right.track  --> [ CARDIAC: lubdub decoder ] --> right --+

