GENERATIVE AI CONTENT
---------------------
Yes. Claude Code was used to help write the Rust code for the various effects
and as a research assistant to help dig up things like Michael Abrash's hints
on how to use VGA Mode X. Claude was also used to help build the supporting
tools:  the HEARTBURN runtime, the rust-cardiac compiler, and the lubdub project
for generating audio. Claude also helped create Blender models, most notably
the Stadium and Blimp models at the end.

UNIQUE PROPERTIES
-----------------
This is the largest CARDIAC application ever created and it's not even close.
It shows that even a tiny computer is capable of great things.  So far as I 
know it marks the first time CARDIAC has been used to generate audio or 
video output. 

RUNNING IT
----------
Open Terminal in this folder and run `./card-attack play`
Sound goes to the Mac's current output device (System Settings > Sound >
Output). Escape quits. README.txt lists the options.

